WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-Thank you, I appreciate that.

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is exciting.
You guys are nice.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:06.006
I did a show recently, there was
a guy in the front row --

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:06.840 line:92%
I thought he looked like me.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Hey, man.
you look like me."

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.577 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And then he went, "Oof."

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.615
I was like, "Well, I didn't mean
to hurt our feelings."

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.384 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a bummer, but I
did realize that's probably

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.421
the best way to get a sense
of what you look like --

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
tell somebody else
they look like you

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.393 size:78% position:39%
and then see how they
immediately respond.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.761 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
You walk up to a stranger,
"You look like me!"

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.665
They're like, "Screw you!"
I'm like, "Damn it, I knew it."

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very self-conscious
about my looks.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got body-shamed
when I was younger.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a new term --
body-shaming.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I was young,
we called it telling a person

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
what they looked
like to their face.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was --

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.113 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.915 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I got -- Thank you.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.284 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.486 line:92%
Yeah, give it up for the '90s!

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.687 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was great.
I got made fun of

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.524
for having a big forehead.
This girl came up to me,

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
she said, "You have
a five-head."

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
At the time,
I'd never heard that term.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"What's a five-head?"

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.365
And she was like,
"Like a forehead, but bigger --

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.367 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a five-head."

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.470
It sucks when you get made fun
of and then the person explains

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
how they made fun of you,
and it's pretty good.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like,
"That's not bad, actually.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's clever."

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
It also sucks --
If you get made fun of

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.514
for being fat that's horrible,
but at least you can be like,

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know what,
I'm gonna diet and exercise,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:24.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and I'll show you."

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.719
But if you're getting made fun
of for having a big forehead,

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's no really no action
for you to take.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't be like, "I'll have
the Caesar salad.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm watching
my forehead right now."

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:38.398
I was pretty smart -- I just
tried to keep my eyebrows raised

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
all of the time.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.168 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.137 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just looked surprised
all through middle school.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.575 line:92%
I'm like, "That's unbelievable!"

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.310 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very body-conscious now.
I go to the gym a lot.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's hard to tell --
I'm wearing long sleeves.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I am pretty
ripped under here.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
My gym's all body-builders.
I don't like the term,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.488
"body-builder."
I feel like it's too exclusive.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
Technically, we're all
body-builders, just some of us

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
are building crappier bodies
than other people.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:07.694 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:08.495 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I like to lift weights.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
My favorite part
of lifting weights

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that break in-between sets
where you kind of

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
check your phone and go home
for a couple of weeks.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's my --

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.702 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.469 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.506 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.342
I'm taking a breather right now,
but I was at the gym

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
the other day --
I saw a guy lifting weights

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.812
in a way I've never seen before.
Have you ever seen this?

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had a thing wrapped
around his head,

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then there was a cord
attached to weights

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.618 line:92%
and he was lifting the weights.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:32.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was screaming.
He was like, "Aah! Aah!"

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.158
I was like, I think we have
different fitness goals.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.995
I was on the elliptical and I'm
like, "That guy's a danger

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to society. What?"

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.999 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think if you get to the
neck portion of your workout,

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.604
you can go ahead and clock out
and head home and hug your dad

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.006 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for the first time.

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.208 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.345 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.181
Also, he was yelling.
I don't really care for the guys

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
that yell at the gym.
You see them like, "Beh! Wah!"

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, I feel like
you need fiber more than

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.021 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you need a workout.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't need
to yell at the gym.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're always
over by the freeway.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's where you see
the yellers -- by the freeway.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
You never really see a guy
on the exercise bike

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:21.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
reading "People" magazine
like, "Aah! Aah!"

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.039
I don't yell.
The loudest noise I've ever made

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.141 line:92%
at the gym is, "hoo," you know?

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
One time I yelled, but it was
for help so I feel like

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was a little
more understandable.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.082 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a true story -- I dropped
some weight on my chest.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't see the one in front
of the 30, so I kind of

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
dropped the weight.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.822 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
Luckily, the neck guy,
he was nearby.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
He came over,
he scooped it right off.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just shot it off.
I was like, "Oh, thank you."

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:53.600 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.835
I work out of hotels a lot.
I stay in a lot of hotels.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.303 size:88% position:44%
I was a hotel recently,
I had an awkward moment.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a hot tub and
I was sitting in the hot tub,

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.674
and I wasn't wearing my glasses
'cause I'd just been swimming.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.310
You can't swim with glasses on.
You'll look like a psychopath.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
So...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was sitting in
the hot tub, no glasses,

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.817
and then these two beautiful
women, they came and got into

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
the hot tub with me
and without thinking,

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got out of the hot tub,
put my glasses on,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then came back
into the hot tub.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:21.060 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.731
That's really one of
the creepiest things you can do

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:26.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
within the law,
because there's no reason

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:30.069
to go get your glasses that
moment, other than to look at

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.738 size:84% position:42% line:92%
these women, obviously.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
I tried to pretend
I was reading the rules.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "I wanna see
if we can horseplay.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.878
I thought it might be fun
if we all horseplayed."

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:39.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:42.048
And then, my glasses started to
fog up, which is even creepier

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're like --
[ imitates glass squeaking ]

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.685 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Laughs nervously ]

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are great.
Thank you very much.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
My name's Joe List.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Band plays ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's what I'm talking
about there!

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.762
That's how to do it, pal!
Look, a standing ovation!

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:58.131 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.465 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Joe List, everybody!

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can follow Joe on Twitter
@JoeListComedy.

